more of its revenue from one customer during the year.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"group_structure":{"title":"Related (RHP)","body":"[{\"name\": \"Jagatjit Industries Ltd\", \"relation\": \"related party\", \"note\": \"Enterprise over which KMP/major shareholder is able to exercise significant influence.\"}, {\"name\": \"Pashupati Properties P. Ltd\", \"relation\": \"related party\", \"note\": \"Enterprise over which KMP/major shareholder is able to …","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"capex_expansion":{"title":"Expansion (RHP)","body":"The Company continues to pursue its long-term vision of becoming a significant player in the Indian dairy industry, with emphasis on capacity expansion, product innovation, and market penetration. The Company aims to leverage industry opportunities by innovating and diversifying its product portfolio.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"risks":{"title":"Risks (RHP)","body":"- Prices of the main raw material, loose ghee, fluctuate frequently due to volatility in raw milk prices; supply and market chains for both are largely in the unorganised sector, so the Company at times pays more for supply and receives less on sales.\n- Liquidity position remained under stress due to an 8% fall in revenue from operations during the year, resulting in negative cash flow from operating activities; the position improved only after disposal of the MBD plant.\n- Exposure to changes in market interest rates relates primarily to the Company's borrowings with floating interest rates; a 1% rate change was shown to affect profit before tax by Rs 124 Lakhs (FY26) / Rs 117 Lakhs (FY25).\n- Contingent liabilities include disputed Goods and Service Tax demands (including a Moradabad Plant GST demand) and a reopened Income Tax assessment for AY 2019-20 alleging escapement of income of Rs 2,230 Lakhs, both contested by the Company.\n- The Company has received 10% or more of its revenue from one customer during the year, per its segment reporting disclosure.\n- Management flags declining interest among rural youth in dairy farming as a risk to the milk supply base.\n- Limited testing infrastructure in government labs creates uncertainty in food safety compliance for the Company.","src":"drhp","as_of":""}},"scorecard":{},"concallIntel":{},"segments":[],"themes":[],"ipo":{"summary":{},"analysis":{}},"coverage":{"concall":false,"deepDive":false,"drhp":true,"projection":false,"stage":false},"pageModel":{"schemaVersion":"company-page/1.0","layout":"vertical","identity":{"symbol":"MLKFOOD","name":"MILKFOOD LTD.","sector":"Fast Moving Consumer Goods","industry":"Food Products"},"coverage":{"deepDive":false,"drhp":true,"stage":false,"priceHistory":true,"themes":false,"concall":false},"adapters":{"deepDive":{"available":false,"profile":"none","sections":{}},"drhp":{"available":true,"structured":true,"profile":"drhp","sections":{"case":true,"business":true,"financials":true,"execution":false,"ownership":true,"risks":true,"peers":true,"listing":false,"verdict":false}}},"hero":{"oneLiner":"Milkfood Limited is a single-segment dairy products manufacturer producing Ghee and Milk Powder.","businessQuality":null,"sector":"Fast Moving Consumer Goods","industry":"Food Products"},"sections":[{"id":"business","label":"Business","renderer":"drhpBusiness","available":true,"completeness":"full","sourceType":"drhp"},{"id":"case","label":"Investment Case","renderer":"drhpGenericCase","available":true,"completeness":"full","sourceType":"drhp"},{"id":"peers","label":"Industry & Peers","renderer":"drhpGenericPeers","available":true,"completeness":"full","sourceType":"drhp"},{"id":"financials","label":"Financials","renderer":"drhpFinancials","available":true,"completeness":"full","sourceType":"drhp"},{"id":"stage","label":"Stage Analysis","renderer":"stage","available":true,"completeness":"partial","sourceType":"momentum"},{"id":"ownership","label":"Ownership & Governance","renderer":"drhpOwnership","available":true,"completeness":"full","sourceType":"drhp"},{"id":"risk